#. i18n: file kmyfirewallwizard.ui line 96
#: rc.cpp:136
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<html><head><meta name=\"qrichtext\" content=\"1\" /></head>"
"<body style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:helvetica\">\n"
"<p><span style=\"font-weight:600\">This Wizard tries to make it as easy as "
"possible to setup a quite-tight iptables firewall for home and office use. "
"</span></p>\n"
"<p>KMyFirewall will setup an iptables firewall for you that follows the main "
"rule \"don't let anything in that has nothing to do with the things I'm "
"doing\"; actually, when a new packet arrives at your host the kernel will have "
"a look at its headers to decide whether the packet is an answer to a packet you "
"sent, or if it is another host trying to connect to your computer. </p>\n"
"<p>Further, you can setup a ruleset that also restricts access to the Internet; "
"this may be useful for office hosts where you do not want people to use "
"unauthorized services (e.g. Chat). Most of the common Internet services can be "
"activated by a single click; for others you have to specify the port number(s) "
"that it uses to enable access to them. </p>\n"
"<p>For hosts that also provide services, e.g. a web server (Apache), you have "
"to enable those services by activating them in the \"Incoming Connections\" tab "
"because, by default, nobody is allowed access. </p>\n"
"<p><span style=\"font-weight:600\">The ruleset generated by this Wizard is only "
"based on the INPUT and the OUTPUT chains of the \"filter\" table, so IP "
"Forwarding will be deactivated (for details see: man iptables). The main part "
"of the filtering is done by the connection-tracking module so you will need to "
"have either the modules \"ip_conntrack\" and \"ipt_state\" loaded or built-into "
"your running kernel. </span></p>\n"
"<p>If you are thinking about setting up a router you will need to use the "
"advanced Interface to setup a firewall that also uses the routing functionality "
"of the kernel; to do this click \"Cancel\" then \"Settings -&gt; Configure "
"KMyFirewall\" to begin setting up your ruleset. </p>\n"
"<p>For a simple firewall that will protect more-than-adequately for a normal "
"workstation, just click \"Next &gt;\" five times and then \"Finish\": this will "
"install the default configuration, which should work quite well for a simple "
"workstation without any public services running on it.</p>\n"
"</body></html>\n"
msgstr ""

